  "summary": "Traditional Portuguese jewelry featuring intricate filigree work in the shape of a heart with a cross.",
  "description": "Characterized by delicate silver threads forming ornate patterns, symbolizing love and faith; developed from ancient metalworking techniques, becoming a national symbol of Portuguese craftsmanship.",
  "culturalContext": "Though filigree has become a special branch of jewellery in modern times, it was historically part of the ordinary work of the jeweller. Indeed, all the jewellery of the Etruscans and Greeks (other than that intended for the grave, and therefore of an unsubstantial character) was made by soldering together and so building up the gold rather than by chiselling or engraving the material.",
